<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ljubljana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Laibach</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ljubljana is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, on the Ljubljanica river. The Roman colony of Emona stood on its site, and as Laibach it was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carniola">Carniola</a>. It served as the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyrian-provinces">Illyrian Provinces</a> from 1809 to 1813 and hosted the Congress of Laibach in 1821, and in 1991 it became the capital of independent Slovenia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ljubljana.jpg" alt="Ljubljana" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrew Milligan Sumo · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ljubljana_Old_Town,_Slovenia_(Old_Camera)_(33286165680).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
